<Layouts.app flash={@flash} current_scope={@current_scope}>
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold">Aurora Meter, in an application</h1>

  <p>
    This is the reference application for <a href="https://hexdocs.pm/aurora_meter" class="link">Aurora Meter</a>. It meters
    usage, enforces a plan's quotas, holds and settles prepaid credit, records a
    durable fact for every unit of work, and stages that fact for export, and it does
    all of it in about six hundred lines you can read.
  </p>

  <div class="alert alert-info" role="note">
    <div>
      <p><strong>There is no AI here and there is no payment here.</strong></p>
      <p class="text-sm">
        The workload is a deterministic simulation: no account, no key, no network
        call. Credit is granted by the seed or from the developer tools page and is
        labelled synthetic wherever it appears. Nothing on any page takes money or
        says that money was taken.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6">What to look at</h2>
  <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
    <li>
      <strong>/generate</strong>
      is the whole teaching path: a quota that reserves, a credit hold for an
      estimate, the work, a durable record, a settlement for the real cost.
      Double-click the button and watch it be refused.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>/history</strong>
      lines up the three identities of one request: the local row, the durable event
      and the credit hold.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>/ops</strong>
      is the operator's view: the conservation identity, the credit lots in spend
      order, the outbox, and the two reporting sources side by side.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6">Signing in</h2>
  <p :if={@current_scope && @current_scope.user}>
    You are signed in. <.link navigate={~p"/generate"} class="link">Start generating</.link>.
  </p>
  <p :if={is_nil(@current_scope) || is_nil(@current_scope.user)}>
    Run <code>mix sample.seed</code>, then
    <.link navigate={~p"/users/log-in"} class="link">log in</.link>
    with one of the seeded accounts it prints. It logs in by emailed link and the
    mail is in the local mailbox at <code>/dev/mailbox</code>.
  </p>
</Layouts.app>
